## Non-weapon actions: archery, fishing, gardening, handling and survival
## gestures. Durations for existing kinds match ActionFrames.DURATIONS.
## Field reference: res://Forest/keeper/KeeperMotion.gd
##
## Archery contract (BowController): the bow sits in the MAIN hand and "ta" is
## the stave axis - the controller draws the string from the tips at
## grip +- dir(ta) * 6 px to the OFF hand, and nocks the arrow at the off
## hand. So the stave stays square to the aim (profile ta -90, front 0, back
## -180) and the off hand starts at the grip and pulls the string back past
## it (away from the target) over bow_draw; frame 7 is the full-draw pose the
## controller holds while the button is down. bow_release lets the drawing
## hand spring back while the string snaps straight (release flash), then
## lowers the bow.
## Fishing contract (FishingController): the line leaves the rod tip at
## hand + dir(ta) * rod reach. Rod angles sit on the sprite's 15-degree
## rotation steps (source -47.3 + 15k) so the drawn tip and the line agree.
## fishing_cast ends in exactly the pose fishing_reel loops from.

